Move frontend-observable display settings, custom themes, keybinding state, project-trust presentation, Mermaid configuration and startup overview into focused canonical data/projection domains, using the ownership audit to keep permission policy and filesystem authority in the backend. Begin with app/tui/interactive_tui.cpp, startup_overview.*, mermaid_tui_bridge.*, runtime.h, runtime_state.* and runtime_views.*. Backend publishers expose neutral facts; frontend projections create labels, formatted strings and local views. Do not transport ProjectTrustSnapshot or StartupOverviewSnapshot merely under a different name.

Reload actions publish changed canonical values and return only necessary success/error/applied-versus-unchanged control information. Preserve effective setting precedence, atomic reload semantics, preview/cancel behavior and generation-based invalidation. Refreshing a display string must not consume a pending behavioral change such as image visibility, cursor style or Mermaid configuration. Keep external rendering/image capabilities separate from presentation state. Failure must leave prior valid state intact and deliver actionable error feedback.

Remove migrated options/snapshot fields and redundant callback payloads once their consumers use TuiFrontEnd projection refreshes. Verify trust changes, settings reload unchanged/success/failure, theme preview and persistence, image toggling, cursor and Mermaid refresh, and startup overview opening/closing across sessions. Use deterministic state/render tests plus relevant startup/settings terminal smokes, recording what actually ran.
